","",40.89,34.55],"haran":["Haran","",39.032,36.864]},"stops":[{"p":"urofthecha","ref":"Genesis 11:27-31","note":"Terah's family lived here. Terah took Abram, Sarai and Lot and set out for Canaan."},{"p":"babylon","ref":"Genesis 11:31","note":"Genesis does not name the stops. Travellers usually followed the Euphrates north, past Babylon.","way":1,"path":[[46.104,30.962],[44.49,31.66],[44.421,32.536]],"mi":167},{"p":"mari","ref":"Genesis 11:31","note":"A large city on the middle Euphrates in this period. A likely point on the river road.","way":1,"path":[[44.421,32.536],[42.93,33.53],[42.42,34.02],[42.34,34.35],[42.14,34.28],[41.78,34.52],[40.89,34.55]],"mi":268},{"p":"haran","ref":"Genesis 11:31-32","note":"They settled in Haran instead of going on. Terah died here.","path":[[40.89,34.55],[39.81,35.74],[39.09,35.88],[39.032,36.864]],"mi":212}],"bbox":[39.032,30.962,46.104,36.864],"relief":{"src":"bible/fact/relief_mesop.jpg","box":[31,28,49,40]}},"abram2":{"title":"Abram: Haran to Canaan","refs":"Genesis 12","when":"Patriarchs. Dates debated","miles":424,"note":"Likely route along the trade road through Damascus. Approximate.","debated":false,"places":{"haran":["Haran","",39.032,36.864],"aleppo":["Aleppo","",37.16,36.2],"damascus":["Damascus","",36.313,33.519],"shechem":["Shechem","",35.282,32.214]},"stops":[{"p":"haran","ref":"Genesis 12:1-5","note":"God called Abram to leave for a land he would show him. Abram was 75 when he set out."},{"p":"aleppo","ref":"Genesis 12:5","note":"Not named in Genesis. A likely point on the trade road south.","way":1,"path":[[39.032,36.864],[38.016,36.829],[37.16,36.2]],"mi":121},{"p":"damascus","ref":"Genesis 15:2","note":"Not named on this trip, but Abram's servant Eliezer came from Damascus.","way":1,"path":[[37.16,36.2],[36.386,34.353],[36.313,33.519]],"mi":193},{"p":"shechem","ref":"Genesis 12:6-7","note":"At the oak of Moreh God promised the land to Abram's offspring. Abram built an altar.","path":[[36.313,33.519],[35.6,32.9],[