ary gave birth to her firstborn son and laid him in a manger.","path":[[35.444,31.871],[35.235,31.777],[35.207,31.705]],"mi":19}],"bbox":[35.207,31.705,35.55,32.707],"relief":{"src":"bible/fact/relief_levant.jpg","box":[30,26,39,35]}},"egypt":{"title":"The flight into Egypt","refs":"Matthew 2","when":"about 6–4 BC","miles":274,"note":"Where they stayed in Egypt is not named. Shown to On (Heliopolis). Approximate.","debated":false,"places":{"bethlehem":["Bethlehem","",35.207,31.705],"gaza":["Gaza","",34.433,31.525],"pelusium":["Pelusium","",32.55,31.04],"on":["On","",31.338,30.108]},"stops":[{"p":"bethlehem","ref":"Matthew 2:13-14","note":"An angel warned Joseph in a dream. He took the child and his mother by night."},{"p":"gaza","ref":"Matthew 2:14","note":"Not named in Matthew. The coast road to Egypt ran through Gaza.","way":1,"path":[[35.207,31.705],[35.094,31.536],[34.8,31.4],[34.433,31.525]],"mi":56},{"p":"pelusium","ref":"Matthew 2:14","note":"Not named in Matthew. A border town at the edge of Egypt.","way":1,"path":[[34.433,31.525],[33.8,31.13],[32.55,31.04]],"mi":120},{"p":"on","ref":"Matthew 2:14-15","note":"Matthew does not say where they stayed. On (Heliopolis) is shown as one possibility.","way":1,"path":[[32.55,31.04],[31.338,30.108]],"mi":97}],"bbox":[31.338,30.108,35.207,31.705],"relief":{"src":"bible/fact/relief_levant.jpg","box":[30,26,39,35]}},"paul1":{"title":"Paul's first journey","refs":"Acts 13–14","when":"about AD 46–48","miles":1504,"note":"By road and by sea, measured along the routes in Theo’s atlas. Approximate.","debated":false,"places":{"antiochs":["Antioch","in Syria",36.165,36.201],"seleucia":["Seleucia","",35.938,36.117],"salamis":["Salamis","",33.903,35.179],"paphos":["Paphos","",32.408,34.76],"perga":["Perga","",30.854,36.961],"antiochp":["Antioch","in Pisidia",31.189,38.306],"iconium":["Iconium","",32.492,37.872],"lystra":["Lystra","",32.338,37.602],"derbe":["Derbe","",33.361,37.349],"attalia":["Attalia","",30.705,36.884]},"stops":[{"p":"antiochs","ref":"Acts 13:1-3","note":"The church set apart Barnabas and Saul for the work. Believers were first called Christians here (Acts 11:26)."},{"p":"seleucia","ref":"Acts 13:4","note":"Antioch's harbour on the coast. From here they sailed for Cyprus.","path":[[36.168,36.199],[36.08,36.108],[35.942,36.123]],"mi":16},{"p":"salamis","ref":"Acts 13:5","note":"The main city on the east coast of Cyprus, Barnabas's home island (Acts 4:36). They preached in the synagogues. John Mark helped them.","path":[[35.942,36.123],[34.93,36.103],[34.591,35.636],[33.914,35.178]],"mi":143,"sea":1},{"p":"paphos","ref":"Acts 13:6-12","note":"Seat of the Roman governor, Sergius Paulus, who believed. From here on, Luke calls Saul by the name Paul.","path":[[33.903,35.179],[33.956,35.122],[33.781,34.991],[33.658,34.962],[33.541,34.813],[33.358,34.735],[32.943,34.652],[32.729,34.711],[32.609,34.685],[32.408,34.76]],"mi":106},{"p":"perga","ref":"Acts 13:13","note":"John Mark left them here and went back to Jerusalem.","path":[[32.408,34.76],[32.306,34.898],[32.249,35.081],[32.3,35.097],[32.283,35.852],[31.389,36.758],[30.767,36.761],[30.702,36.897],[30.854,36.962]],"mi":213,"sea":1},{"p":"antiochp","ref":"Acts 13:14-52","note":"Paul's first recorded sermon. Many Gentiles believed. Opposition drove them out of the region.","path":[[30.857,36.967],[30.721,36.992],[30.58,37.209],[30.128,37.466],[30.05,37.685],[30.363,37.989],[30.798,38.274],[31.022,38.331],[31.178,38.302]],"mi":150},{"p":"iconium","ref":"Acts 14:1-6","note":"A great number of Jews and Greeks believed. When a plot to stone them formed, they fled.","path":[[31.182,38.3],[31.497,37.959],[31.717,37.863],[31.955,37.901],[32.064,37.858],[32.217,37.899],[32.492,37.869]],"mi":87},{"p":"lystra","ref":"Acts 14:8-20","note":"Paul healed a man lame from birth. The crowd called them gods. Later Paul was stoned and left for dead.","path":[[32.492,37.869],[32.348,37.592]],"mi":21},{"p":"derbe","ref":"Acts 14:20-21","note":"They made many disciples. Then they turned back the way they came.","path":[[32.347,37.592],[32.571,37.195],[32.784,37.27],[33.233,37.183],[33.377,37.338]],"mi":82},{"p":"lystra","ref":"Acts 14:21-22","note":"They strengthened the disciples and urged them to remain true to the faith.","ret":1,"path":[[33.377,37.338],[33.233,37.183],[32.784,37.27],[32.571,37.195],[32.347,37.592]],"mi":82},{"p":"iconium","ref":"Acts 14:21-22","note":"They encouraged the believers to keep the faith through hardship.","ret":1,"path":[[32.348,37.592],[32.492,37.869]],"mi":21},{"p":"antiochp","ref":"Acts 14:21-23","note":"They appointed elders in each church, with prayer and fasting.","ret":1,"path":[[32.492,37.869],[32.217,37.899],[32.064,37.858],[31.955,37.901],[31.717,37.863],[31.497,37.959],[31.182,38.3]],"mi":87},{"p":"perga","ref":"Acts 14:24-25","note":"This time they preached the word in Perga.","ret":1,"path":[[31.178,38.302],[31.022,38.331],[30.798,38.274],[30.363,37.989],[30.05,37.685],[30.128,37.466],[30.58,37.209],[30.721,36.992],[30.857,36.967]],"mi":150},{"p":"attalia","ref":"Acts 14:25-26","note":"The port where they boarded a ship for Syria.","ret":1,"path":[[30.854,36.962],[30.705,36.884]],"mi":10},{"p":"antiochs","ref":"Acts 14:26-28","note":"They gathered the church and reported how God had opened a door of faith to the Gentiles.","ret":1,"path":[[30.705,36.884],[30.854,36.962],[30.702,36.897],[30.767,36.762],[31.389,36.758],[31.725,36.591],[32.472,36.075],[32.801,36.013],[33.688,36.113],[33.941,36.199],[34.087,36.309],[34.157,36.46],[35.569,36.45],[35.92,36.122],[36.056,36.1],[36.168,36.199]],"mi":372,"sea":1}],"bbox":[30.05,34.652,36.168,38.331],"relief":{"src":"bible/fact/relief_aegean.jpg","box":[19,29,44,43]}},"paul2":{"title":"Paul's second journey","refs":"Acts 15–18","when":"about AD 49–52","miles":3001,"note":"By road and by sea, measured along the routes in Theo’s atlas. Approximate.","debated":false,"places":{"antiochs":["Antioch","in Syria",36.165,36.201],"derbe"